      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path (45%):</strong> Both declaratory positions are at maximum hardness; parliament Hormuz governance bill advancing toward plenary at p=0.55 (N2) would institutionalize closure in domestic law; Iranian kinetic activity on Omani coast approaches continued through the reporting period; IAEA nuclear inspections remain blocked; MOU window expires in 3 days with no extension framework.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (40%):</strong> Neither side has committed to decisive kinetic escalation beyond current enforcement levels; China and Russia diplomatic engagement continues; economic pressure remains a bilateral constraint; the Pezeshkian administration maintains diplomatic-track optics even while unable to override SNSC policy.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (15%):</strong> Anchored on F4 at p=0.15; requires reversal of all CONTRADICTED indicators plus Iranian acceptance of an enrichment cap — no signal of any reversal in the current cycle; the 76-day F4 horizon provides the only residual probability mass.</p>
